2.1 FL Systems
Federated learning, with its nature advantages in privacy-preserving decision sharing, has garnered significant attention in both industry and academia, leading to the rapid development of federated learning systems. The earliest attempt at the large-scale FL system was by Google, where FL was used to improve next-word prediction [77] and query suggestion [245] for Gboard applications. Subsequently, many novel FL systems have

